// WHY: asserts that `wait sleepBlocking(...)` still triggers the "`wait` has no effect"
// warning after the sleepMs→sleepBlocking rename. The check.rs:1716 list must contain
// "sleepBlocking" — if the rename was applied to the dispatch arm but not to the
// redundant-wait CPU-only-intrinsic list, this warning silently stops firing.
// sleepBlocking blocks the OS thread; the `wait` keyword has no effect on it.
function entrypoint() -> nothing {
  wait sleepBlocking(100)
  print(`done`)
}
